{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/319700-how-to-merits-work-for-covers","id":319700,"title":"How to merits work for covers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-23T00:51:34-08:00","id":319700,"title":"How to merits work for covers","content":"How do Merits work when you get a new cover.<br /> <br /> I wanted to know something about pacts. One of my players is currently making a deal with a military man for his military background ad the demon will bring his friend who died back to life. <br /> <br /> So here is the thing. The guy got kicked out of the military after an officer accidentally shot his friend. The military man killed his commanding office which got him kicked out the military. Luckily no jail time.<br /> <br /> Now here is my question. Being that the player is bring back this guy best friend from the dead would that change no only his friend dying but also make it so that the military man never got kicked out of the military ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","user":"Basic","date":". 11-23-2014, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T04:20:20-08:00","id":319800,"title":"","content":"I'll answer your question with a question: how is he bringing the dude back to life?<br /> <br /> This is, to my knowledge, beyond the capacity of an Asset for a pact; resurrection is beyond a mere Merit. The main means of doing so I can think of would be the Raise Dead Exploit, which doesn't alter time retroactively, so if he's using that, then no, everything that's happened would still have happened the same way up to the current time, when the previously dead friend would then climb back up healthy and alive, but in a world that thinks (correctly) that he died years ago.<br /> <br /> In turn, the demon would acquire the man's military background and everything associated with it \u2014 which means the demon is now known to have shot that officer and gotten a dishonorable discharge. To complicate things further, if the military man met that friend in the military rather than beforehand, giving the demon his military background means the demon is now the person who befriended the resurrected friend, not the military man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T09:57:24-08:00","id":320001,"title":"","content":"So what can pacts do ??<br /> <br /> I thought they could bring some one back from the dead","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T11:41:50-08:00","id":320089,"title":"","content":"The relevant pages of the corebook are pp. 192-193, specifically the Benefits header and section on the Asset benefit, and the sidebar Where Does the Money Come From?<br /> <br /> For a signatory, a pact can yield, basically, up to approximately five experiences' worth of stuff a mortal human could normally buy on his own. The mechanism underlying pact benefits is unclear even to the demons involved, but it seems to work through preexisting structures in reality. If you're making the dude rich, then coincidences stack up - he finds a lost wallet, say, or wins the lottery. If you're making him fit, his metabolism seems to shape up. Pact benefits do subtle work you could explain away \u2014 they don't work miracles.<br /> <br /> A pact can involve miracles, but the demon's going to have to work the miracle herself, and just have the pact stipulate that the demon's end of the contract requires her to resurrect the dead. You can do a lot with Embeds and Exploits; they're not subject to the restrictions on pact benefits. You just have to put in the legwork.<br /> <br /> For the demon's end, the pact works a little heavier. Facets of identity exchanged through a demonic pact take on retroactive qualities. Filed paperwork changes to match the new deal; loved ones recognize the demon as the person in the relationship rather than the signatory; bowling buddies remember having bowled with the demon, conflating the demon's actions with the past actions of the signatory. It works on a sort of &quot;path of least resistance&quot; basis, however; the pact alters reality as little as necessary to make the relationship fit its new owner, maintaining as much history as possible intact. You're trading for the relationship the signatory has, not a significantly altered form of that relationship.<br /> <br /> Pacts don't make new things. They shuffle around existing things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T19:18:53-08:00","id":320308,"title":"","content":"Unlike Stupid Loserman, I don\u2019t have a problem with the notion of using a pact to bring someone back to life; I\u2019d treat it as an example of the mortal bargaining for an Ally Asset, where he\u2019s quite specific about who the Ally is to be. Bear in mind that if the pact gets broken, the friend goes back to the grave. I\u2019m OK with the notion of Pacts themselves working miracles on both sides of the bargain, not just for the demon. <br /> <br /> That said, I agree with him that the mortal can\u2019t bargain away something that he doesn\u2019t have when he signs the Pact; so the demon would pick up a ruined military career from the bargain. The reason why the military career was ruined will change to account for it being part of the demon\u2019s Cover and for the Asset not being dead; but it will still be in tatters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T19:30:59-08:00","id":320309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/319700-how-to-merits-work-for-covers?p=320001#post320001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what can pacts do ??<br /> <br /> I thought they could bring some one back from the dead</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree in part with Dataweaver about using a pact to bring someone back to life mostly because of the fact that if you are the storyteller, you should do what you feel is best for the game, even if it involves stretching what a pact can actually do a tad bit.<br /> <br /> If you are going by the corebook as it is written, then this would be beyond what a demon could do. For Demons (and not Inferno demons), the benefit of a pact such as this is the demon gains a very strong cover to hide from the god machine, while the other person gains an asset such as merit dots or skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T20:10:00-08:00","id":320322,"title":"","content":"Actually, I\u2019m not even sure it would be impossible according to the rules as written. The Pact rules in the core book certainly don\u2019t require the demon to \u201cdo the legwork\u201d to give someone the Asset; the sidebar about \u201cwhere does the money come from?\u201d certainly carries the implication that signing the contract is all the demon needs to do to make its effects real. As well, the book says nothing about what Merits a mortal can pick up from a Pact; only that some are internal and others are external, and that some sort of \u201ccosmic balance\u201d seems to be preserved when granting external Assets. More to the point, there\u2019s nothing saying that a mortal must ask for \u201can Ally\u201d and then leave the details to be filled in by the pact; he can and should be able to specify <i>who he wants</i> as his Ally. <br /> <br /> Whether or not this could be used to bring someone back from the dead strikes me as a gray area that\u2019s best resolved by the individual Storyteller; my argument is that it probably <i>could</i>, by specifying that you want the person who has died to be a living, breathing Ally. It\u2019s also possible that asking for this would result in the friend coming back as a ghost or zombie, if the Storyteller wants to allow the Pact to go forward but doesn\u2019t like giving demons the power to annul death. <br /> <br /> I would note, though, that if you <i>do</i> allow Pacts to undo someone\u2019s death, the aforementioned \u201ccosmic balance\u201d factor is likely to kick in, taking someone else\u2019s life in the place of the life of the person who is no longer dead. <br /> <br /> Bottom line, it\u2019s very definitely a decision that ought to be made based on the needs of the story first, and of a legalese reading of the rules second if at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T22:47:56-08:00","id":320417,"title":"","content":"That being said, in demon, knowing a guy who knows a guy can very well include people who can make retcons, the resurrection of the dead, or cloning with mind uploads depending on the infrastructure they might have subverted or carried off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T19:44:11-08:00","id":327582,"title":"","content":"I think Loserman has the right of it. I my game I would require the demon to have the proper exploit for the whole thing to work. Then again I would also make this a soul contract, life for a life, because the cosmic ledger needs balancing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T20:42:00-08:00","id":327646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/319700-how-to-merits-work-for-covers?p=320417#post320417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That being said, in demon, knowing a guy who knows a guy can very well include people who can make retcons, the resurrection of the dead, or cloning with mind uploads depending on the infrastructure they might have subverted or carried off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes; but I\u2019ve seen nothing in the text that says that such a thing is needed. If a demon wants to make a pact (lowercase-p) with a mortal that doesn\u2019t have any metaphysical weight behind it, he certainly can; and in <i>that</i> case, he needs to \u201cdo the legwork\u201d to satisfy his ned of the bargain; but so does the mortal with whom he made the deal. If he puts metaphysical weight behind it and makes it a supernatural Pact, that\u2019s a whole different story: the mortal doesn\u2019t have to do anything beyond signing the contract to hand over bits of his life to the demon; so why should the demon have to do anything beyond signing the contract to grant the benefits that the mortal asked for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T21:27:45-08:00","id":327679,"title":"","content":"I would say because there's a subtle difference between adjusting lottery probability and pulling a soul back to this world while restoring a body to perfect health (from a several year stint in decay).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}